      "math_academy_id": "q-348693",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e520dc67-3b63-5ca7-959b-f642d85529d6",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Magnitude of a Vector-Valued Function",
      "problem": "Given that $r(t)=\u27e8\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t),\\,\\sqrt{t+3},\\,t-1\u27e9,$ what is $|r(1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =\u27e8\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi ),\\,\\sqrt{4},\\,0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-1,\\,2,\\,0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
